{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong multimodal baseline while testing the central hypothesis that combining RNA and image modalities outperforms either alone. config_002 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion) tests this hypothesis with a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200 captures biological structure better than PCA but is cheaper than scGPT) and a strong pretrained image encoder (ViT-L). Singleprofile avoids aggregation overhead, keeping cost moderate. This configuration sits in the middle of the design space, so the result will be informative in multiple directions: if it performs well, I can explore multiprofile aggregation, scGPT, and concat fusion as extensions; if it underperforms, I can diagnose whether the RNA encoder, image encoder, or fusion strategy is the bottleneck. Expected relative cost: moderate (~60-70% of the most expensive configs like scGPT+ViT-L+transformer aggregation), since scvi_n200 is a lightweight VAE and there is no multiprofile aggregation step, though ViT-L adds significant compute."
}

